            {"note_id": "FCT_0275", "quote": "Students are asked to use what they have learned in this section to build a mortgage calculator."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0276", "quote": "When the program runs, it asks a few questions."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0277", "quote": "The first question asks for the principal, or the amount of loan."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0278", "quote": "Example principal value: $100,000."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0280", "quote": "Example interest rate: 3.92%."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0013", "quote": "The third question asks for the period in years."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0014", "quote": "Example period: 30 years."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0281", "quote": "We need to multiply this number by 12 (months in a year) to calculate the number of payments."},
            {"note_id": "FCT_0286", "quote": "Monthly interest is calculated by taking the annual interest, dividing it by percent, and then dividing by months in a year."}
